{"author":{"id":"1d21e70a32f794e19f8d3626c963a95c52102f79bd1dc44e2b4b611903f1b863"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1781094887,"nonce":"4TkESniWI+MKSGudr18XZRsMhMo=","target":"8f34a1755261651f041cd898ed1ffc3882ca5bd31fc2a647dbede6ba6278c8a4","message":"The Perfect Commit\n==================\n\nIdeally each commit should package implementation, tests, documentation, and a link to the issue.\n\nTests\n-----\n\nThis feels kind of difficult for Nix config - we can configure NixOS VM tests at most.\n\nDocumentation\n-------------\n\nThe repo should definitely include a `docs/` or `wiki/` directory that is updated alongside the implementations as a reference and guide for what was added.\nNote that this should be human-written as much as possible primarily to avoid overly verbose documentation.\n\nThis is a disciplinary issue - I have added the docs/ folder and will endeavour to update it.\n\nIssues\n------\n`git-bug` works great, however I was unable to push to the git remote due to this error: \n\n```sh\nError: ssh: handshake failed: ssh: unable to authenticate, attempted methods [none publickey], no supported methods remain\n```\n\nThe cause of this issue (investigated by Claudius) is that the SSH library that `git-bug` uses only supports authentication with the ssh-agent, not falling back to the SSH key. Thusly, I implemented user services to run `ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519` on login. This didn't work right away on NixOS, as I had to also point SSH_AUTH_SOCK in the service config environment to `%t/ssh-agent`, which is how the NixOS option `programs.ssh.startAgent` persists its agent.\n\nThe TUI is also more ergonomic than the shell commands, so I added `gb` to alias to `git-bug termui`, as well as `gu` and `gy` pulling and pushing for git-bug. Also, I added a custom module to `starship` that will show a 🐛 whenever `git-bug` is out of sync with the remote by diffing `refs/bugs` against `refs/remotes/origin/bugs`.\n\nReferences\n----------\n\n- https://simonwillison.net/2022/Oct/29/the-perfect-commit","files":null}]}